From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: Disable constant buffer streaming for StarCraft II.

StarCraft II intermittently hangs the GPU on RADV with an RX 5700 XT
using GE-Proton11-7. Replacing only DXVK with the GE-Proton10-34 version
avoids the failure. Disabling descriptor heaps and descriptor buffers was
not sufficient, but the reporter now reports success with only
d3d9.deviceLocalConstantBuffers = False on the newer build.

Disable constant buffer streaming in the application profile for SC2.exe
and SC2_x64.exe. Leave descriptor selection, Battle.net, other games and
the global default unchanged. User configuration can still override this
application default. This is a targeted compatibility workaround; the
underlying DXVK/driver failure has not been bisected to a specific commit.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/790
---
diff --git a/src/util/config/config.cpp b/src/util/config/config.cpp
--- a/src/util/config/config.cpp
+++ b/src/util/config/config.cpp
@@ -534,6 +534,10 @@
     }} },
 
+    /* StarCraft II: avoid GPU hangs with constant buffer streaming. */
+    { R"(\\SC2(_x64)?\.exe$)", {{
+      { "d3d9.deviceLocalConstantBuffers", "False" },
+    }} },
     /* A Hat in Time                              */
     { R"(\\HatinTimeGame\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d9.lenientClear",                "True" },
     }} },
